From 827223a37f262e7cd12ab7b04ff647db858c90d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:15:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 60/60] panvk/jm: device-wide workgroup memory, give varying
 memory back

Memory measured in NieR:Automata (Winlator, DXVK) on the Kirin 990: the
driver held ~550 MiB, the phone dropped to 0.46 GB free.

- Workgroup local storage is device-wide, like thread local storage
  already is (jm-v7 118). The vertex/tiler and compute chains of a
  device run one atom at a time on job slot 1 and fragment jobs use
  none, so batches never use it at the same time. Per command buffer
  NieR held 103 MiB of it over DXVK's command buffers; now ~2 MiB.
  PANVK_JM_DEV_WLS=0 restores the per-command-buffer buffers.
- The indirect varying buffers (one per overlap half) grow on GPU page
  faults to the largest batch they served and kept those pages (NieR:
  143 + 225 MiB, in menus too). When no atom is in flight, each check
  interval a buffer above 32 MiB is cut to half (16 MiB minimum); if it
  has grown back to 3/4 of its size by the next check the interval
  doubles (10 s up to 160 s), else it halves (jm-v7 119).
  PANVK_V7_VARY_TRIM=0 turns it off. Checked with a benchmark drawing
  ~180 MiB of varyings per frame: cut and regrown repeatedly, the last
  frame draws the same as the first, no GPU faults.
- GPU profile: the physical memory of the growable buffers (tiler heaps,
  varyings per half, tessellation), next to the reserved sizes.

CTS regression sample: 18 846 pass, the two known cases.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
